<title>TURKEY: Turk Koc Hldg 9-mth profits up 94 pct.</title>
<headline>Turk Koc Hldg 9-mth profits up 94 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jan-Sept 1996 provisional</p>
<p>(billion lira unless stated)</p>
<p>    Per share profit (lira)	  501.09  vs     430.73</p>
<p>    Net profit			 5,010.92  vs   2,580.42</p>
<p>    Operating loss		     337.77  vs	58.85</p>
<p>    Exceptional income	     6,335.36  vs   3,234.34</p>
<p>    Interest paid			  0     vs	 0</p>
<p>    Total debts			2,188.43  vs   1,898.51</p>
<p>    Equity			    21,539.15  vs  11,462.08</p>
<p>    Capital			   10,000.00  vs   5,990.75</p>
<p>NOTE - Koc Holding A.S. is the parent company of Turkey's leading industrial conglomerate.</p>
<p>The figures above do not take into account Turkey's 79.3 percent year-on-year consumer price inflation in September.</p>
<p>-- Istanbul newsroom +90-212-2750875</p>
</text>
